<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="034" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-20 negative canary (NFR-04) — impersonation-inertness merge gate, authored BEFORE the swap</title>
    <phase>1 One evaluator</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <status-note>2026-10-03 — COMPLETED. The manual live gate PASSED on dev: all four live tests green with SPAARKE_CANARY_REQUIRED=true and the existing non-admin user uac.child.user (impersonated 59 vs app-only 61; expected set derived app-only from Deep BU1 ownership plus POA); the inversion check against an admin user FAILED as designed (INERT, 61 = 61); the README records the manual-gate decision, the existing-user variant and the two credential variables the run needs; the 005/007/008 checklist is recorded in note section 5. Evidence: notes/task-034-negative-canary.md section 8. Task 036 is unblocked. 2026-09-30 — DECISION BLOCK LIFTED (see the amendments block at the end of this file): both owner decisions below are now resolved by standing owner directives. The status stays blocked-shipped ONLY until the manual live run passes; nothing is waiting on an owner decision any more. 2026-09-03 — mechanism SHIPPED and perturbation-proven; the LIVE run is blocked on two owner decisions (provision a non-admin canary user; choose scheduled-canary vs CI-secrets). Both POML escalation triggers fired legitimately. Decision record: notes/task-034-negative-canary.md. Task 036 MUST NOT proceed until the canary runs truthfully against a provisioned user.</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>TEST-MODIFYING override (modifies tests/**, tags testing/integration-test) — code-review + adr-check unconditional; also auth tags.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Complex but FULLY specified — the exact test design (assertions, fixtures, fail direction) is written verbatim in investigation 08 §3d; literal execution is what's wanted.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>p1-independent</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>testing, integration-test, auth, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the negative canary for Dataverse impersonation as a BLOCKING MERGE GATE (spec NFR-04), and land it BEFORE the FR-20 swap (task 036 lists this task as a gate dependency). The fail-OPEN failure mode it guards: an impersonation header silently not applied yields the app-only (System Administrator) row set with HTTP 200 and no error — org-wide disclosure with zero symptoms. The canary makes that state a loud build failure: an impersonated low-privilege read must return a STRICT SUBSET of, and STRICTLY FEWER rows than, the same query app-only. Equality means impersonation is inert and the build fails. This is a merge gate, not a nice-to-have.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, integration testing against live Dataverse. Follow ADRs strictly (ADR-038 KEEP-path seam test).</role>
  <goal>tests/integration/auth/ImpersonationNegativeCanaryTests.cs implementing Tests 1-3 from investigation 08 §3d, wired into CI as a required (blocking) check for the access path; canary-user provisioning contract documented so the fixture is reproducible per environment.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Investigation 08 §3: DataverseImpersonation.Apply silently no-ops on null/Guid.Empty BY DESIGN; the read primitive guards its own entry (throws on Guid.Empty, DataverseWebApiService.cs:962-965) but app-only is the silent default of the whole client — any new call path that forgets to pass the id compiles fine and runs app-only. The canary is the only mechanism that catches "header not applied" (proxy stripping, privilege revoked, wrong parameter) regardless of cause. Canary design verbatim: CanaryUser = permanently-provisioned low-privilege systemuser (User-level Read on sprk_matter only; owns exactly K seeded matters; org contains &gt;K matters it cannot read). Spec NFR-04 gates Phase 1 on this test.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/ImpersonationNegativeCanaryTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/README.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Communication/DataverseImpersonationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/ExternalAccess/StandingGrantRuntimeUnionSeamTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-04">Scope: the canary assertions. Test 1 MUST assert BOTH impersonatedIds ⊂ appOnlyIds AND impersonatedIds.Count &lt; appOnlyIds.Count (strictly fewer). Equality is a FAILURE — never a skip, never a warning. Do not weaken to non-strict subset.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: test placement and style. tests/integration/auth/** is a KEEP path; write behavioral tests against the real primitive — no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-01">Scope: fixture failure handling. A missing/misconfigured canary user must FAIL the run with an actionable message (which user, which privilege, which seed count) — never silently skip, because a skipped canary is an open gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this task. Do NOT modify src/server/** — the canary tests the EXISTING primitive (RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync). If the primitive needs a change to be testable, that is an escalation, not an edit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-005">ADD to this task's live-tenant verification checklist (you are the first task that has a real tenant). Task 005 replaced the "can I retrieve the record -> therefore Read" probe with Dataverse's RetrievePrincipalAccess, but NO test exercises that HTTP call -- mocking the transport is ADR-038 ban B1, so the URL form and its availability under a delegated (OBO) token can ONLY be settled against a real tenant. The comment task 005 deleted claimed RPA "may not be available" under OBO; that claim was unverified (zero call sites -- nothing had ever exercised it), and the old probe was retained as a fallback precisely because it could not be settled offline. While you have the tenant: (a) confirm a caller holding Write/Create on a record gets those flags in the snapshot, not just Read; (b) grep the BFF logs for the RPA-FALLBACK marker -- if it is firing, the Read ceiling is silently BACK and every Write+ operation denies while looking like a legitimate insufficient_rights; (c) confirm the BFF application user holds the privileges RPA needs on the app-only path (read systemuser + read the target). This is observation only -- it does NOT require modifying src/server/**, so it does not conflict with the constraint above. Rationale: notes/task-005-rights-mapping.md section 8. Scope: this task's live-tenant verification checklist.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-008">SCOPE EXPANSION of the task-005 RPA obligation above -- read it first, then this. Task 008 made RetrievePrincipalAccess the gate for SIX external-access MUTATION endpoints (grant, invite, invite-and-grant, revoke, close-project, provision-project), not just the document read path. CallerRecordAccessProbe issues OBO WhoAmI() then RetrievePrincipalAccess against sprk_projects / sprk_matters / sprk_workassignments -- a DIFFERENT target entity from task 005's sprk_documents, so 005 passing does NOT imply 008 passes. There is deliberately NO read-probe fallback here (a read proves Read, and Read is not licence to grant), so if RPA is unavailable under a delegated token every external-access mutation returns 403 and the Manage Access UI is dead rather than merely degraded. While you have the tenant: (a) confirm WhoAmI() returns the CALLER's systemuserid under an OBO Dataverse token; (b) confirm RetrievePrincipalAccess answers for a sprk_project target, not only sprk_documents; (c) grep the BFF logs for BOTH markers -- RPA-FALLBACK (read path, silently caps at Read) and DELEGATION-RPA-UNAVAILABLE (mutation path, denies outright). Observation only; no src/server/** change. Rationale: notes/task-008-delegation-rule.md sections 3 and 9. Scope: this task's live-tenant verification checklist.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-007">ADD to this task's live-tenant verification checklist. Task 007 added the expiry predicate "(sprk_expiresdate eq null or sprk_expiresdate ge {yyyy-MM-dd})" to three grant read paths, but its tests assert the QUERY STRING only -- ExternalParticipationService talks to Dataverse through a raw HttpClient, so proving Dataverse honours the filter offline would need a transport mock (ADR-038 ban B1). sprk_expiresdate is DATE ONLY (verified via metadata), which makes the comparison semantics worth confirming empirically. While you have the tenant, verify all three: (a) a grant with an expiry in the PAST disappears from GET /api/v1/external/me; (b) a grant expiring TODAY still confers access -- this is the "ge not gt" decision, and getting it wrong shortens every dated grant in the system by a day; (c) a grant with NO expiry is completely unaffected -- if this one fails the eq null branch is broken and external access is DOWN for nearly everyone, so check it first. Also confirm no 400 is being returned: a 400 on this query surfaces as an EMPTY grant set, i.e. a silent access outage rather than an error. Observation only; no src/server change. Rationale: notes/task-007-grant-expiry.md sections 3 and 6. Scope: this task's live-tenant verification checklist.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse impersonation, fail-OPEN detection, integration seam tests</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/08-option-b-feasibility.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="live-Dataverse seam test" location="tests/integration/seam/ExternalAccess/StandingGrantRuntimeUnionSeamTests.cs">The existing seam-test harness (config-driven live environment, seeded records, cleanup) is the fixture style to copy for the canary.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Read investigation 08 §3 in full; inspect the integration test harness conventions (existing tests/integration/** fixtures, environment config).</step>
    <step order="1">Define the canary-user fixture contract in tests/integration/auth/README.md: exact security-role shape (User-level Read on sprk_matter ONLY), K seeded matters owned by the canary, the invariant that the org holds &gt;K matters, and the config keys the tests read (canary systemuserid, expected seed ids). Include the provisioning steps an operator runs once per environment.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement Test 1 (strict subset + strictly fewer — the header-not-applied catcher), Test 2 (exactness: impersonatedIds == the K seeded ids), Test 3 (integration assertion that RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync with Guid.Empty throws — pins the guard so a refactor cannot drop it).</step>
    <step order="3">Wire the tests into the CI pipeline as a blocking check for access-path changes (follow the repo's existing integration-test CI wiring; if integration tests are not run in CI today, wire this class into whatever gate DOES block merges and record the mechanism in the README).</step>
    <step order="4">Run against dev; verify all three pass with the provisioned canary user, and verify Test 1 FAILS if pointed at an admin-privileged user (manual one-time inversion check — record the evidence in notes).</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document deviations + the inversion-check evidence in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If no non-admin canary user can be provisioned in dev (spec Prerequisites: isolation is not verifiable from an admin account — an admin sees every record by definition, making the strict-fewer assertion structurally unsatisfiable), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6: the FR-20 swap (task 036) MUST NOT proceed until the canary can run truthfully.</trigger>
    <trigger>If CI has no mechanism to run live-Dataverse tests as a blocking check, STOP and escalate with options (scheduled canary + required manual gate vs. secrets provisioning for CI) rather than silently landing the tests as non-blocking.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Impersonation unit contract tests exist (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Communication/DataverseImpersonationTests.cs) but only pin Apply()'s no-op contract against mocks — nothing exercises the live header end-to-end; tests/integration/auth/ does not exist yet (glob verified during authoring).</existing>
    <extension>No — the strict-fewer invariant is only meaningful against live Dataverse row security; it cannot live in the unit suite, and ADR-038 names tests/integration/auth/** as the KEEP path for exactly this seam.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>An impersonation header silently not applied returns the app-only (System Administrator) row set with HTTP 200 — org-wide disclosure with zero symptoms, and the FR-20 swap would ship ungated (spec NFR-04).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/ImpersonationNegativeCanaryTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">tests/integration/auth/README.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Test 1 asserts impersonatedIds ⊂ appOnlyIds AND impersonatedIds.Count strictly &lt; appOnlyIds.Count for the same sprk_matters id-only query; run green against dev with the canary user.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test 2 asserts the impersonated set equals exactly the K seeded matter ids.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test 3 asserts RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync(entitySet, query, Guid.Empty) throws.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with a Global-read caller substituted (inversion check), Test 1 FAILS — evidence recorded in notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with the canary-user config absent, the tests FAIL with an actionable message (not skip, not pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The blocking-gate wiring exists and is documented in tests/integration/auth/README.md; task 036 can cite it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file under src/server/** modified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec NFR-04 + investigation 08 §3d (verbatim design) + register E-4. RESIDUAL (not this task): the RUNTIME canary variant (startup/scheduled strict-fewer check emitting a metric + alarm, guarding production config drift) — recommended by investigation 08, not mandated by NFR-04; file via project-defer-issue-tracking when this task closes.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>

  <amendments date="2026-09-30" source="owner standing directives, session 27 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md, round 2 BINDING)">
    <verdict>THE TWO OPEN DECISIONS ARE RESOLVED. The status stays blocked-shipped until the manual live run
    passes; the DECISION block is lifted. Both escalation triggers fired legitimately on 2026-09-03 and both
    are now answered by the owner, so neither may be re-raised as a reason to wait. The only remaining
    obligation is to perform the manual run truthfully and record it.</verdict>
    <amendment n="1" resolves="escalation trigger 2 (CI mechanism) + step 3 + the CI half of the blocking-gate criterion">
    The live run is a MANUAL gate. No Dataverse test runs in CI (owner 2026-09-10, reaffirmed as a standing
    directive 2026-09-30). Option (A) "scheduled canary with federated credential" and option (B) "Dataverse
    secrets in CI" are both declined; neither may be built under this task. The tenant-free layers that
    already run in CI (the perturbation tests and the config tripwire
    Fr20ImpersonatedRootSetFlag_WhenEnabledInCheckedInConfiguration_RequiresAProvisionedCanary) stay exactly
    as shipped and remain the mechanical half of the gate. The live layer is run by hand, with
    SPAARKE_CANARY_REQUIRED=true, before task 036 merges. Update the section "What is NOT yet wired (open
    decision)" of tests/integration/auth/README.md to record this decision and the manual procedure,
    replacing the open-decision wording.</amendment>
    <amendment n="2" resolves="escalation trigger 1 (no non-admin canary user)">
    Use an EXISTING non-admin test user who already sits in the correct business unit as the canary. Do NOT
    create a new systemuser, do NOT relocate any user between business units, and do NOT build the
    dedicated "Spaarke Impersonation Canary" role. Set SPAARKE_CANARY_SYSTEMUSERID to that user's
    systemuserid (the Dataverse row id, not the Entra oid).
    Consequence for the fixture contract: that user's roles are broader than "User-level Read on
    sprk_matter only", so the provisioning section of the README must be rewritten to describe the
    existing-user variant. Test 1 (strict subset AND strictly fewer) is unchanged and remains the gate.
    Test 2 (exactness) needs SPAARKE_CANARY_SEEDED_MATTER_IDS to equal the set Dataverse should return
    for that user. Derive that expected set independently of the impersonated read (for example from the
    matters that user owns or has shared to them, when the user's sprk_matter read depth is User-level).
    Record in notes how it was derived.</amendment>
    <amendment n="3">The 2026-09-09 hazard still applies: until then every root-BU user inherited System
    Administrator through the root BU's default owner team, so both reads compared equal, which is a
    confident false pass. Before the run, confirm the chosen user holds no role (direct or team-inherited)
    that grants Organization-depth Read on sprk_matter. Record both set sizes (impersonated, app-only) in
    notes/task-034-negative-canary.md.</amendment>
    <amendment n="4">prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser: in dev it is held through the System Administrator role on
    the BFF application users "# mi-bff-api-dev", "SDAP-BFF-SPE-API" and "# Spaarke DMS-SPE Dev 1".
    This was verified by role on 2026-09-30, not by a live call, and no Spaarke role holds it. The manual
    run is the first live proof. A run that fails on the privilege is a failed gate. Do not grant the
    privilege to a Spaarke role as a workaround.</amendment>
    <amendment n="5">The live-tenant checklist carried by the task-005, task-007 and task-008 constraints (RPA
    flags beyond Read; the RPA-FALLBACK and DELEGATION-RPA-UNAVAILABLE log markers; WhoAmI under OBO; RPA on
    a sprk_project target; grant-expiry past, today and none) is executed during the same manual session.
    notes/task-034-negative-canary.md section 5 lists it as NOT PERFORMED. Record each observation there.</amendment>
    <acceptance-criteria-amended>
      <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE: all four live tests (ImpersonatedMatterRead_..._ReturnsAStrictSubsetAndStrictlyFewerRows, ImpersonatedMatterRead_..._ReturnsExactlyTheSeededMatters, RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync_..._RefusesAnEmptyCaller, HelperStampedMatterRead_..._ReturnsAStrictSubsetAndStrictlyFewerRows) run against dev with SPAARKE_CANARY_REQUIRED=true and the existing non-admin test user, and ALL FOUR PASS. None halts as NOT RUN. Both set sizes, the user's role list (direct and team-inherited) and the derivation of SPAARKE_CANARY_SEEDED_MATTER_IDS are recorded in notes/task-034-negative-canary.md.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative (exactness is independent): the expected matter set for Test 2 was derived WITHOUT the impersonated read (for example an app-only query of owner, owning team and principal-object-access rows for that user, filtered by the user's recorded sprk_matter read depth). Setting it by copying the impersonated result is a failed gate.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative: equal sets are recorded as a FAILED gate, never a pass. Task 036 does not merge on that result.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">tests/integration/auth/README.md records the manual-gate decision and the existing-user fixture variant. The "open decision" wording is removed. The CI-blocking tenant-free layers are unchanged.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">No user was created, relocated between business units or re-roled for this run, and no Dataverse credential was added to any .github workflow.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">The task-005, task-007 and task-008 live checklist items each have a recorded observation in notes/task-034-negative-canary.md section 5.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Once all of the above hold, this task's status is set to completed and the TASK-INDEX marker is updated to match (scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 clean for this id).</criterion>
    </acceptance-criteria-amended>
    <escalation-amended>
      <trigger>If no existing non-admin test user in the correct BU can make Test 1 satisfiable (the user can already read every matter, or the org holds no matter outside the user's read scope), STOP and report the user's roles and the two counts. Do not create or relocate a user to fix it, because that contradicts the standing directive.</trigger>
      <trigger>If the existing user's sprk_matter read depth is Business Unit or deeper, or the user reaches matters through team or hierarchy access, so that the Test 2 expected set cannot be derived independently with confidence, STOP and report the roles and the candidate derivation. Recommendation to put to the owner: keep Test 1 (strictly fewer) as the gate and record Test 2 against the best independent derivation, rather than weakening Test 2's assertion. Do not edit the test to pass.</trigger>
      <trigger>If the impersonated set equals the app-only set, STOP. That means impersonation is inert. Escalate with the counts and do not flip any flag.</trigger>
    </escalation-amended>
  </amendments>
</task>
